# The hero's left-facing run body: 10 frames, complete.
#
# The tree already had HERO_RUN_LEFT_ARM_F00..F09 (minus F04) with no body
# family beside it -- an arm series naming frames whose bodies were still
# CV_ placeholders. Inverting the usual direction finds them: each named arm
# frame is co-drawn with exactly ONE unnamed piece, one-to-one across all
# nine, and those pieces are full figures (45..48 tall, 10..11 leaves, bottom
# on the ground) drawn at [HERO_X] only.
#
# F04 is not in the arm family and was placed by three independent lines that
# agree, the same "forced by geometry" standard ../actor-sprite-sheet/ used
# for its two frame-7 gaps:
#
#   position   CV_1474 is drawn by DRAW_CV_297, immediately between
#              DRAW_CV_296 (F03's body, with arm F03) and
#              CAPSULE_HERO_RUN_LEFT_FOOTSTEP_PHASE_2 (F05's body, arm F05)
#   offset     0x13B2 +0xC2-> 0x1474 +0x96-> 0x150A fills a double stride;
#              every other step in the early run is 0xA2..0xAE
#   geometry   48.0x31.0 with 10 leaves, and it is the ONLY live CV in
#              0x13B4..0x150A with a body shape
#
# It draws no arm at all, which is why HERO_RUN_LEFT_ARM_F04 does not exist:
# the arm family's gap is a frame with no arm, not a missing name.
CV_11B8 HERO_RUN_LEFT_BODY_F00
CV_125A HERO_RUN_LEFT_BODY_F01
CV_1304 HERO_RUN_LEFT_BODY_F02
CV_13B2 HERO_RUN_LEFT_BODY_F03
CV_1474 HERO_RUN_LEFT_BODY_F04
CV_150A HERO_RUN_LEFT_BODY_F05
